     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>–38300</p>\n<p>Case 3: The absolute value of the number is 10 or larger.</p>\n<p>Step 1: Count the number of digits that are to the left of the decimal point. Label this <i>n</i>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"n = 5\"></span>\n</p>\n<p>Step 2: Write the digits of the number without the decimal place, if one was present. If the number was negative, include the sign.</p>\n<p>–38300</p>\n<p>Step 3: If there is more than one digit, place the decimal point after the first digit.</p>\n<p>–3.8300</p>\n<p>Step 4: Multiply the number from Step 3 by <span data-math=\"{10^{n - 1}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"- 3.83 \\times {10^4}\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\" - 3.38 \\times {10^4}\"> - 3.38 \\times {10^4}</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 506875,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "0.0045",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>0.0045</p>\n<p>Case 2: The absolute value of the number is less than 1.</p>\n<p>Step 1: Count the number of digits between the decimal and the first non-zero digit. Label this <i>n</i>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"n = 2\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 2: Starting with the first non-zero digit of the number, write the digits. If the number was negative, include the negative sign.</p>\n<p>45</p>\n<p>Step 3: If there is more than one digit, place the decimal after the first digit from Step 2.</p>\n<p>4.5</p>\n<p>Step 4: Multiply the number from 3 by <span data-math=\"{10^{ - \\left( {n + 1} \\right)}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"4.5 \\times {10^{ - \\left( {2 + 1} \\right)}} = 4.5 \\times {10^{ - 3}}\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"4.5 \\times {10^{ - 3}}\">4.5 \\times {10^{ - 3}}</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 506876,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "1",
